From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: sm8450-lpass-lpi: force runtime suspend across system sleep

The sm8450 LPI pin controller has only runtime PM ops, and it is a
device-link supplier of the SoundWire controllers and the LPASS macros.
On the AYANEO Pocket VERT the WCD938x SoundWire masters are kept
runtime-active for jack detection; for system sleep they and the macros
are force-suspended (0563, 0564) but keep their link references, so the
pin controller stays active with its LPASS_HW_MACRO and LPASS_HW_DCODEC
votes. The ADSP then never sleeps and the SoC never reaches AOSD, CXSD or
DDR low power: 0 of 59.6 s, against 98.9% with the masters runtime
suspended. Force the runtime suspend across system sleep, as 0565 does
for the sm8650 driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8450-lpass-lpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8450-lpass-lpi.c
@@ -205,6 +205,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id lpi_pin
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, lpi_pinctrl_of_match);
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops lpi_pinctrl_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(pm_clk_suspend, pm_clk_resume, NULL)
 };
 
